    "prep": {
      "type": "uc-csc-content",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Shipping Container Drop Site Preparation",
        "body": "<p>A big part of shipping container drop-offs is being prepared. When your location is well-suited for drop-off, storage, or transfer, the process can be completed in an hour or less. Here's what to consider before ordering, to save time and avoid safety risks, equipment damage, or delivery cancellation.</p><p><strong>Delivery vehicle & trailer clearance.</strong> Drop sites without sufficient clearance can make it difficult or impossible to perform drop-offs — make sure your site offers enough room to maneuver the vehicle, trailer, and container into place.</p><p><strong>Level ground.</strong> The drop site should be on level ground to ensure secure delivery and even weight distribution across all four corners. If the ground isn't naturally level, it can be modified with stone pavers, blocks of wood, gravel, or railroad ties.</p><p><strong>Drop site ground surfaces.</strong> Containers can be dropped off on any surface that is firm, level, and dry — asphalt or concrete is ideal, though compact dirt, gravel, and even grass may be suitable if level and well-supported. Sand, soft dirt, and muddy ground are not recommended.</p><p><strong>Free of debris and safety hazards.</strong> Make sure your drop site is free of rocks, tree stumps, branches, low-hanging wires, cables, or any other obstacles or hazards.</p><p><strong>Weather conditions.</strong> Plan your delivery around weather forecasts — bad weather can lead to snowy or icy roads, muddy grounds, flooding, and soft soil that may cause delays or cancellation.</p><p><strong>Being ready.</strong> Make sure neighbors are informed, no vehicles or obstacles are in the way, and you or a representative is on-site at the time of arrival to avoid delay fees.</p>",
        "primary_image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1029/2284/6530/files/uc-delivery-container-doors.png?v=1789074149",
        "image_alt": "Shipping container doors close-up"
      }
    },
